  "section_notes": "The final v40 sets a 24-hour reporting deadline for all thermal incidents and a mandatory 8-per-100,000 per-model recall trigger, which is the key exposure for Halcyon's Ember 8 at 9.9. S2 sets a hard 5% cap with sales stopped until verified retesting, which blocks Northwind's Hearth 10 at 6.2% from new placement, while per-model results reach buyers and regulators but are not published. S3 is the only section rated weakened: the 24-month new-unit shut-off deadline is longer than the 12-month acceptable range, while the 6-year retrofit window falls within the acceptable range and favours Northwind's 38% coverage."
